{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Laminar Flow Selection for Thermal Models.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Laminar Flow Selection for Thermal Models.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"laminar flow selection for thermal models laminar flow selection for thermal models","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Laminar Flow Selection for Thermal Models.md","fileName":"Laminar Flow Selection for Thermal Models.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Laminar Flow Selection for Thermal Models","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:55\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Conjugate Heat Transfer Systems]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Conjugate Heat Transfer Systems","Thermal Model Verification and Sensitivity","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Laminar Flow Selection for Thermal Models.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Laminar Flow Selection for Thermal Models.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"laminar flow selection for thermal models laminar flow selection for thermal models","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Laminar Flow Selection for Thermal Models.md","fileName":"Laminar Flow Selection for Thermal Models.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Laminar Flow Selection for Thermal Models","heading":"Laminar Flow Selection for Thermal Models","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A laminar flow model assumes orderly viscous motion without resolving turbulent fluctuations. For internal pipe flow, Reynolds number compares inertia with viscosity and provides a regime check; the book's pipe examples keep the value below about 2,300.\n\nBecause density and viscosity may vary with temperature and pressure, a velocity that begins in the laminar range may not remain there throughout a heated system. [[Thermal Model Verification and Sensitivity|sensitivity checks]] should therefore examine the regime criterion across the solved property range.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Conjugate Heat Transfer Systems","Thermal Model Verification and Sensitivity","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Laminar Flow Selection for Thermal Models.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Laminar Flow Selection for Thermal Models.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"laminar flow selection for thermal models laminar flow selection for thermal models","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Laminar Flow Selection for Thermal Models.md","fileName":"Laminar Flow Selection for Thermal Models.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Laminar Flow Selection for Thermal Models","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Conjugate Heat Transfer Systems","Thermal Model Verification and Sensitivity","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}